From: local <local@gurux-dlms-ts>
Subject: Read a length-prefixed BCD value once its digit bytes have arrived

getBcd waits for twice as many bytes as the BCD value's length, so a
value such as `0d 04 01 40 72 40` (Hexing maximum demand registers) is
reported as incomplete and the read never finishes. Each byte holds two
digits, so the value is complete once `len` bytes remain.

diff --git a/development/src/dlms.c b/development/src/dlms.c
index 8a47dca..7f16171 100644
--- a/development/src/dlms.c
+++ b/development/src/dlms.c
@@ -798,7 +798,7 @@ int getBcd(gxByteBuffer* buff, gxDataInfo* info, unsigned char knownType, dlmsVA
             return DLMS_ERROR_CODE_OUTOFMEMORY;
         }
         // If there is not enough data available.
-        if ((buff->size - buff->position) < (uint16_t)(2 * len))
+        if ((buff->size - buff->position) < len)
         {
             info->complete = 0;
             return 0;
